---
// Placeholder home page. The setup session replaces this with the real one.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Not set up yet" description="This site is waiting for its first setup session.">
  <section class="placeholder">
    <h1>Almost there</h1>
    <p>
      This site hasn't had its setup session yet. Open the folder that holds this
      repository in Claude Code, in the Code tab, and say:
      <strong>“set up my organization”</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The setup goes over your services and connectors with you first, one at a
      time, and publishes your private intranet. Then you'll be interviewed, your
      content will be ingested (drop files in <code>source/inbox/</code>, or point
      at your old site), and a first version of this site will be built with you.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .placeholder {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .placeholder h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .placeholder code {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0 var(--space-1);
    font-size: 0.95em;
  }
</style>
